WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:06.270
Everyone wants to be someone.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.139
We all want a title.

00:00:08.139 --> 00:00:09.139
A status.

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:10.660
A distinction.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.039
Something to give our existence meaning.

00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:18.410
As a child, we are asked what we want to be
when we grow up.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:24.590
We are given the impression that we are not
yet enough and must long for careers and titles

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.020
in order to feel whole.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:33.170
And so we follow this thread, hoping it will
pull our life into meaning.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:38.640
We all have something to contribute, something
to work towards, something to be passionate

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.010
about.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:46.030
But in the process of turning these somethings
into goals and careers, it is important that

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:52.800
we maintain separation between them and our
sense of life and self-worth.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:59.510
If we search for ourselves entirely through
our career goals, we will never be satisfied

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:04.339
with who we find, because career goals never
end.

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:10.570
Instead, we must remember that we are all
intrinsically worth as much as what we decide

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.440
we are worth.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:19.230
Every human is an individual with value and
wonder in their spirit, and no career achievement,

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:23.940
or lack there of, can determine otherwise.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:29.420
When we are young, we should be asked what
we want to DO when we are older, not who we

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.570
want to BE.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:37.550
For who we are is who we are, with or without
career achievements.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:43.740
The moments of our childhood are not worth
less than the moments of our adulthood just

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:48.460
because we did not yet have a career or status.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:55.710
Our ability to create meaning and enjoy our
self is often the strongest as a child, and

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:02.770
we must remember that we can continue to carry
this with us all through life, independent

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:06.659
of our careers and statuses.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:14.280
When we acknowledge our intrinsic value, regardless
of status, we become like a tree, grounded

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.280
and full of life.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:23.010
And our career accomplishments become like
fruit growing from our limbs, providing nutrients

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:34.069
for 

00:02:34.069 --> 00:02:37.920
the world.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:44.510
Our careers and accomplishments are certainly
major parts of our lives that we should appreciate

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:51.520
and take pride in, but if you neglect to embrace
your self-worth and sense of life outside

00:02:51.520 --> 00:03:11.319
of them, you have missed 

00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:17.950
the point.

